course: dictionary
lesson: 4056
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Genesis» is a good example. With a capital G, it is the name of a book in the Bible. With a small g, «the genesis of an idea» means how the idea began.
explain: Read the words around the word first. «Genesis 1 says God made man and woman in his own image» has a chapter number, so Genesis must be a book. «The genesis of an idea» has no chapter number, and the words idea and began tell you it means a beginning.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «the beginning of an idea» still make sense? Yes, so the small-g meaning fits. Capital letters, numbers and small clues like these help you choose the right meaning.
fact: Genesis, with a capital G, is the first book of the Bible.
fact: Genesis, with a small g, means the beginning, or where something came from.
fact: «The genesis of a plan» means how the plan began.
fact: Genesis tells the creation story: God makes the world in six days and rests on the seventh.
fact: Genesis also holds the stories of Adam and Eve, Noah's ark and Joseph.
exercise: «Genesis 1 says God made man and woman in his own image.» What is Genesis here? | A street in a town | *The first book of the Bible | A type of tree | A cake from the bakery
exercise: Mia reads, «The genesis of the plan was a sketch on a napkin.» What does genesis mean here? | *How the plan began | A sketch on a napkin | A kind of paper | The end of the plan
exercise: Which clue shows that Genesis in «in Genesis» is the name of a book? | The word plan | Nothing, you can't tell | *The capital G and the word in before it, not a small g | The capital G and the word in before it
test: Which word is a synonym for genesis meaning beginning? | Middle | *Origin | Finish | Ending
test: Adam and Eve hid «because I was afraid». Which book of the Bible tells this story? | Psalms | *Genesis | Ruth | Revelation
exam: Which sentence uses genesis to mean a beginning? | Genesis is a sweet treat sold in the shop | Genesis is my dog's name | *Every good invention has a genesis, a first spark of an idea | The genesis of the sea is a film about fish
